---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeTabs from '../../components/CodeTabs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icons.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'before-you-start', text: 'Before you start' },
  { id: 'step-1', text: 'Choose a provider key' },
  { id: 'step-2', text: 'Search the live web' },
  { id: 'step-3', text: 'Read the cited answer' },
  { id: 'step-4', text: 'Add to an agent' },
];

const requests = [
  {
    label: 'cURL',
    lang: 'bash',
    code: `curl -X POST "$XWEB_BASE/api/v1/search" \\
  -H "X-XWeb-Key: $TAVILY_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "query": "What is the latest on the Model Context Protocol?",
    "max_results": 5,
    "include_answer": true
  }'`,
  },
  {
    label: 'JavaScript',
    lang: 'javascript',
    code: `const response = await fetch(\${XWEB_BASE} + "/api/v1/search", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "X-XWeb-Key": process.env.TAVILY_API_KEY,
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    query: "What is the latest on the Model Context Protocol?",
    max_results: 5,
    include_answer: true,
  }),
});
const search = await response.json();
console.log(search.answer?.text, search.answer?.citations);`,
  },
];

const agentSnippet = `async function webSearch(query) {
  const response = await fetch(\${XWEB_BASE} + "/api/v1/search", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
      "X-XWeb-Key": process.env.TAVILY_API_KEY,
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      query,
      max_results: 5,
      include_answer: true,
    }),
  });

  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(await response.text());
  const data = await response.json();
  return {
    answer: data.answer?.text,
    citations: data.answer?.citations,
    results: data.results,
  };
}`;
---

<Docs
  title="Quickstart"
  description="Call the real x-web search pipeline from your app or AI agent."
  toc={toc}
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <h2 id="before-you-start">Before you start</h2>
  <p>
    You need a key for a supported search provider: Tavily, Brave Search, Serper or Exa. x-web
    currently proxies your provider key server-side; x-web account keys, subscriptions and billing
    will come later.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>A server-side runtime that can make HTTP requests.</li>
    <li>A key from one of the supported search providers.</li>
    <li>Your x-web deployment URL as <code>XWEB_BASE</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout type="warning" title="Never expose provider keys in browser code">
    Call x-web from your server or agent backend. Do not put the provider key in a public JavaScript
    bundle, mobile app or checked-in source file. The API key is used for this request and is not
    persisted as an x-web account credential.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="step-1">Step 1 — Choose a provider key</h2>
  <p>
    Get a key directly from your chosen provider and set it as a server environment variable. The
    value is sent as <code>X-XWeb-Key</code>; <code>Authorization: Bearer …</code> also works.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="bash"
    title="server environment"
    code={`export XWEB_BASE="https://your-x-web-deployment.vercel.app"
export TAVILY_API_KEY="tvly-…"`}
  />

  <h2 id="step-2">Step 2 — Search the live web</h2>
  <p>Both examples call the deployed API; use the one that fits your backend.</p>
  <CodeTabs tabs={requests} />
  <p>
    For current results, ask naturally (“latest”, “today”, “this week”) or set <code>time_range</code>
    to <code>day</code>, <code>week</code>, <code>month</code> or <code>year</code>. The API detects
    query language by default; pass a language code to override it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="step-3">Step 3 — Read the cited answer</h2>
  <p>
    <code>answer</code> is an object, not a plain string. It contains the answer text, the synthesis
    mode actually used, confidence and citation metadata. Follow the citations to verify claims.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="json"
    title="response (trimmed)"
    code={`{
  "object": "search",
  "query": "What is the latest on MCP?",
  "provider": "tavily",
  "answer": {
    "text": "… [1]",
    "mode": "provider",
    "confidence": 0.7,
    "citations": [{
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Model Context Protocol",
      "url": "https://…",
      "result": 0
    }]
  },
  "results": [{
    "title": "Model Context Protocol",
    "url": "https://…",
    "snippet": "…",
    "published_date": "2026-10-16T…Z"
  }],
  "language": { "requested": "auto", "resolved": "en", "detected": { "code": "en" } },
  "intent": { "type": "news", "time_sensitive": true },
  "meta": { "effective_query": "latest mcp", "rewritten": true }
}`}
  />
  <Callout type="note" title="Answer modes are explicit">
    <code>llm</code> means a configured OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic model synthesized the answer.
    <code>provider</code> means the search provider supplied it. <code>extractive</code> means x-web
    selected relevant sentences and attached citations. Add an answer-model key on the server if you
    specifically need LLM synthesis.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="step-4">Step 4 — Add it to your agent</h2>
  <p>Register this server-side function as a tool in your agent framework:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="javascript" title="web-search-tool.js" code={agentSnippet} />
  <p>
    The response includes <code>intent</code> (what x-web inferred), <code>language</code>, live
    <code>results</code> and optional <code>extracted</code> page text. See the
    <a href="/docs/api">API reference</a> for the full request/response contract and standalone
    intent and extraction endpoints.
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50/70 p-6">
    <span class="ring-gradient grid h-11 w-11 place-items-center rounded-xl text-white">
      <Icon name="rocket" class="h-5 w-5" />
    </span>
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <p class="font-semibold text-brand-900">Try a real search right now</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-600">The playground uses your own key through the server-side proxy.</p>
    </div>
    <a href="/docs/api#playground" class="btn-primary btn-sm">Open playground</a>
  </div>
</Docs>
